"""
Session Scheduler Lambda
Handles session CRUD operations and EventBridge scheduling for automatic ECS start/stop.

API Routes:
- POST   /sessions         - Create new session (schedules EventBridge rules)
- GET    /sessions         - List all sessions
- GET    /sessions/{id}    - Get session by ID
- PUT    /sessions/{id}    - Update session
- DELETE /sessions/{id}    - Delete session (removes EventBridge rules)
- POST   /sessions/{id}/start - Manually start session (triggers ECS)
- POST   /sessions/{id}/stop  - Manually stop session (stops ECS)

Environment Variables:
- SESSION_TABLE: DynamoDB table for session configs (default: v2_SessionConfig)
- DRIVER_TABLE: DynamoDB table for driver configs (default: v2_DriverConfig)
- ACTIVE_SESSIONS_TABLE: DynamoDB table for active sessions (default: v2_ActiveSessions)
- ECS_CLUSTER: ECS cluster name
- ECS_TASK_DEFINITION: ECS task definition name
- ECS_SUBNETS: Comma-separated subnet IDs
- ECS_SECURITY_GROUPS: Comma-separated security group IDs
- SCHEDULER_LAMBDA_ARN: ARN of this Lambda (for EventBridge targets)

Driver Config Schema:
{
    "driver_id": "driver01",
    "driver_name": "Colton Herta",
    "driver_number": "26",
    "team": "Andretti Global",
    "stream_url": "http://stream.example.com/driver01/stream.m3u8",  # M3U8 stream URL
    "driver_address": "192.168.1.100:8080",  # Driver device/radio address
    "is_active": true
}
"""

